/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:26:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:27:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:28:- The full straight line is a mirror axis; the real objects are identified
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:29:  structurally as the only solid rectangles confined to one side, while
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:30:  scattered pixels are noise that may be overwritten inside the corridor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:31:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:32:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:33:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:34:<reference_puzzle index="2" source="train" puzzle_id="1190bc91" lines="36-49">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:35:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:36:Complete a sparse grid by casting occluding diagonal rays from the longest run and filling the remaining diagonal-connected regions from the short bars.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:37:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:38:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:39:- Black-background grid with one unique longest 4-connected foreground object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:40:- The longest object is a horizontal or vertical multicolor run; all other foreground objects are shorter monochrome bars.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:41:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:42:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:43:- On a blank canvas, process the longest run from left to right or top to bottom; each pixel emits four 45-degree rays that stop at the first already-painted pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:44:- Each remaining monochrome bar fills every still-blank pixel reachable from it by diagonal steps.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:45:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:46:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:47:- Earlier pixels in the long run occlude later diagonal rays, and those ray barriers partition the background into diagonal-connected regions for the short bars.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:48:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:49:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:50:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:51:<reference_puzzle index="3" source="train" puzzle_id="689c358e" lines="72-88">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:52:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:53:Mark each arrow-like sprite's pointed frame endpoint with its color and the opposite endpoint black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:54:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:55:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:56:- The grid has a one-pixel solid rectangular frame around a dominant interior background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:57:- Inside the frame are monochrome six-pixel sprites shaped as asymmetric T arrows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:58:- Each sprite has a length-4 bar and a length-3 crossbar one cell closer to the pointed end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:59:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:60:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:61:- For each sprite, follow its bar axis from the shorter end to the frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:62:- Paint that frame endpoint with the sprite color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:63:- Paint the opposite endpoint on the same row or column black.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:64:- Leave the interior background, sprites, and all other frame pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:65:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:66:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:67:- The direction is encoded by the crossbar's off-center position: the nearer end is the pointing end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:68:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:69:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:70:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:71:<reference_puzzle index="4" source="eval" puzzle_id="f560132c" lines="259-273">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:72:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:73:Assemble scattered jigsaw pieces into a rectangle, recoloring each by a legend sprite's color map.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:74:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:75:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:76:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:77:- Several monochrome non-bg sprites (the "pieces"), scattered across the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:78:- One sprite is the legend: it contains a multi-color k×k patch (typically 2×2) encoding output colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:79:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:80:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:81:- Tile all pieces (rotations/reflections allowed) into a tight rectangle with no gaps.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:82:- The legend's k×k color patch defines a spatial color map over the rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:83:- Each piece is recolored to the legend-map color corresponding to its position in the assembled rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:84:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:85:Key insight: The legend piece doubles as both a jigsaw piece and a color key — its internal k×k palette assigns colors by spatial quadrant.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:86:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:87:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:88:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:89:<reference_puzzle index="5" source="train" puzzle_id="98c475bf" lines="62-76">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:90:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:91:Erase the complete interior glyph and expand each endpoint marker pair into its color's full glyph.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:92:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:93:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:94:- The grid is 20x20 with background inside two same-color full-height vertical frame bars.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:95:- Inside the frame there is one complete color glyph and one or more other colors appearing only as two endpoint markers in the same row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:96:- Marker endpoints are always in the first and last interior columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:97:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:98:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:99:- Keep the vertical frame unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:100:- Erase any complete interior glyph.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:101:- For each endpoint marker pair, use that marker color's learned glyph template and anchor its horizontal bar on the marker row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:102:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:103:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:104:- Color identifies which glyph shape to draw; the two endpoint pixels are not copied objects, they are anchors for reconstructing that color's full symbol.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:105:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:106:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:107:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:108:<reference_puzzle index="6" source="eval" puzzle_id="8b7bacbf" lines="42-56">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:109:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:110:Fill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:111:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:112:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:113:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:114:- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:115:- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:116:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:117:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:118:- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:119:- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:120:- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:121:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:122:Key insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:123:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:124:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:125:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:126:<reference_puzzle index="7" source="eval" puzzle_id="abc82100" lines="70-86">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:127:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:128:Use local source-target-pattern examples to replace matching source pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:129:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:130:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:131:- Black background with isolated colored pixels and teal (8) pattern components.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:132:- A rule example is a 4-neighbor colored pair source->target whose continued
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:133:  direction reaches an anchor touching a teal pattern component.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:134:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:135:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:136:- For each rule example, copy that teal component onto every other pixel of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:137:  source.color, recoloring the copied component to target.color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:138:- Translation maps the rule anchor onto the source pixel being replaced.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:139:- Remove teal components and all pixels used by rule examples.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:140:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:141:Key insight: The two adjacent colored pixels define the color substitution and
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:142:the anchor point; the nearby teal component is the stencil that gets recolored.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:143:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:144:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:145:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:146:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="train" puzzle_id="a6953f00" lines="45-63">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:147:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:148:Extract the top-left or top-right 2x2 corner crop selected by the top edge clue.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:149:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:150:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:151:- The input is a square color grid whose answer is one of the two 2x2 crops
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:152:  touching the top edge and a grid corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:153:- A repeated color on the top row, when present, acts as the primary side cue.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:154:- Otherwise, the two top corner colors have different whole-grid frequencies.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:155:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:156:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:157:- If a top-row color repeats, find the repeated top-row occurrence nearest to
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:158:  a left or right edge and take the 2x2 top-corner crop on that side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:159:- If the top row has no repeated color, compare the whole-grid frequencies of
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:160:  the two top-corner colors and take the side whose corner color is rarer.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:161:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:162:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:163:- The task is not asking for an arbitrary 2x2 search: the decisive information
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:164:  is on the top edge, and it selects which top corner crop to keep.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:165:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:166:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:167:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:168:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="train" puzzle_id="7e4d4f7c" lines="9-24">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:169:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:170:Compress the L-shaped cue to three rows and add a pink copy of the top-row foreground mask.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:171:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:172:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:173:The grid has a dominant background color, a two-color top row, and all
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:174:foreground pixels below the top row lie in the first column as vertical markers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:175:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:176:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:177:Keep the input top row as output row 0 and the first marker row as output row 1.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:178:Output row 2 is background except at the top-row foreground columns, which are
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:179:recolored pink.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:180:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:181:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:182:The lower repeated marker rows only identify the vertical cue; the generated
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:183:row is a recolored mask of the horizontal cue in the top row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:184:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:185:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:186:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:187:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="train" puzzle_id="99caaf76" lines="56-75">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:188:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:189:Move each marked cross object away from its marker to the grid edge while rotating the colored cross 180 degrees.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:190:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:191:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:192:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:193:- Each 8-connected foreground object has nine pixels: a 4-pixel marker-color
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:194:  sprite attached to a 5-pixel non-marker colored cross.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:195:- Each object bbox is either 3x6 or 6x3, so the marker sprite is on exactly
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:196:  one side of the cross.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:197:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:198:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:199:- Move the whole object straight away from its marker side until the object
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:200:  bbox touches the corresponding grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:201:- Keep the marker sprite unchanged within the object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:202:- Rotate the 3x3 colored cross block by 180 degrees before placing it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:203:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:204:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:205:The marker sprite is a directional tail; the cross is the leading payload,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:206:and only that payload turns around during the slide to the edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:207:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:208:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:209:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:210:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="train" puzzle_id="6ffe8f07" lines="49-64">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:211:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:212:Cast yellow horizontal and vertical rays from the teal rectangle until blue blockers stop them.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:213:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:214:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:215:- A black-background grid containing one solid teal rectangle.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:216:- Blue objects are blockers; other non-background objects may lie in the ray paths.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:217:- Yellow is absent from the input and is the output paint color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:218:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:219:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:220:- From every row of the teal rectangle, cast rays left and right to the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:221:- From every column of the teal rectangle, cast rays up and down to the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:222:- A ray stops before a blue pixel; all crossed non-blue, non-teal pixels become yellow.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:223:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:224:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:225:The teal rectangle defines a full cross-shaped projection, while blue objects are walls and red/background cells are simply paintable space.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:226:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:227:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:228:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:229:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="train" puzzle_id="edcc2ff0" lines="47-63">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:230:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:231:Keep only the lower-panel colors named by the top markers and expand each marker into an object-count bar.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:232:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:233:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:234:A black instruction strip sits above a non-black rectangular scene panel.  The strip contains one-cell markers
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:235:in the first column, and each marker color is a candidate object color in the lower panel.  The lower panel has
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:236:a unique dominant background color and scattered 4-connected foreground objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:237:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:238:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:239:In the lower panel, preserve objects whose colors appear as top markers and recolor every other foreground
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:240:object to the panel background.  In the instruction strip, replace each marker by a horizontal run from column 0
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:241:whose length is the number of 4-connected lower-panel objects of that marker color; erase markers with count 0.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:242:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:243:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:244:The top strip is a color filter plus a compact count summary: marker colors select which lower-panel objects
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:245:survive, and their bars report the number of surviving objects by color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:246:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:247:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:248:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:249:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="train" puzzle_id="ecb67b6d" lines="138-155">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:250:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:251:Recolor the grey diagonal-chain regions in an orange field to teal.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:252:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:253:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:254:The input contains only grey pixels and orange pixels.  Grey pixels form
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:255:several 8-connected regions embedded in the orange field.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:256:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:257:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:258:Decompose each grey 8-connected region into 4-connected lobes.  Recolor the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:259:whole region teal only when it contains a straight diagonal run of at least
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:260:three pixels and those lobes meet only by diagonal corner contacts in a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:261:non-branching diagonal chain or cycle; a single 4-connected region is
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:262:recolored only when it is a square diagonal staircase.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:263:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:264:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:265:The teal regions are not selected by size or position; they are the grey
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:266:regions whose internal connectivity depends on diagonal corner joins, while
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:267:same-edge cracks, rectangles, bars, and branching/noisy regions remain grey.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:268:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:269:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:270:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:271:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="train" puzzle_id="5b37cb25" lines="59-73">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:272:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:273:Fill each plus-shaped background notch with the color of the frame side it opens toward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:274:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:275:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:276:- A one-cell-thick rectangular frame has four solid-colored sides and neutral corner pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:277:- The frame interior contains a dominant background color and one foreground object color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:278:- Some object boundaries contain five-pixel plus-shaped background notches.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:279:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:280:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:281:- Find every background plus whose opposite side is supported by foreground object pixels and whose open side faces one frame side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:282:- Recolor the five pixels of that plus with the color of the facing frame side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:283:- Leave all other pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:284:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:285:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:286:The frame side colors are direction labels for the open notches in the foreground object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:287:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:288:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:289:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:290:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="train" puzzle_id="15660dd6" lines="33-54">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:291:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:292:Combine each column's repeated template mask with its single solid color swatch.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:293:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:294:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:295:- The grid is a table of framed panels separated by background rows/columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:296:- The leftmost column gives one solid row-label color for each panel row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:297:- In each panel column, exactly one panel has a solid non-background interior,
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:298:  while the other panels share the same mask drawn in one template color on
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:299:  the background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:300:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:301:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:302:- For every panel column, find the row containing the solid interior swatch.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:303:- Rebuild one output panel using that row's left label as the frame color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:304:- Fill the repeated template mask with the swatch color and leave the mask
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:305:  background cells as background; separate rebuilt panels with one
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:306:  background column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:307:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:308:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:309:The table encodes a colorized stencil per column: the solid panel supplies
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:310:the paint color and frame label, while the duplicate template panels supply
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:311:the shape mask.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:312:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:313:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:314:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:315:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="eval" puzzle_id="8f3a5a89" lines="22-36">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:316:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:317:Paint an inner border around the region reachable from a corner marker pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:318:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:319:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:320:- bg = most common color; wall color (blue) forms barriers dividing the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:321:- A unique single pixel (magenta) sits on one corner — the start marker.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:322:- Some wall-colored pixels are structural (border-touching, enclosing regions); others are decorations.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:323:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:324:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:325:- Flood-fill from the marker corner to find all reachable bg cells, blocked by structural walls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:326:- Erase wall-colored decorations hidden behind structural walls (not reachable from marker side).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:327:- Paint orange (color 7) on every reachable bg cell adjacent to a wall or grid edge — forming a 1-cell inner border.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:328:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:329:Key insight: Only border-connected wall components act as real barriers; interior wall fragments are decorations to be removed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:330:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:331:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:332:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:333:<reference_puzzle index="17" source="train" puzzle_id="c3fa4749" lines="79-96">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:334:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:335:Recolor each side-marked multicolor object embedded in a monochrome panel to its marker color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:336:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:337:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:338:- Same-color 4-connected components form monochrome panel regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:339:- The bounding box of a panel may contain 4-connected non-panel-color objects.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:340:- A target object touches exactly one side of its panel bbox, and all of its
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:341:  pixels on that side have one marker color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:342:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:343:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:344:- For every target object, fill any panel-colored holes enclosed by the object.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:345:- Recolor the object and filled holes to the side marker color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:346:- Leave all other pixels unchanged.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:347:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:348:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:349:- A multicolor object's single contact side identifies both which object should
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:350:  be normalized and which color should replace it.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:351:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:352:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:353:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:354:<reference_puzzle index="18" source="eval" puzzle_id="28a6681f" lines="8-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:355:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:356:Simulate water pixels falling under gravity into basins formed by colored obstacles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:357:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:358:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:359:- bg = 0. Water pixels = color 1 (blue).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:360:- Other colors form static solid structures (walls, steps, containers).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:361:- Water starts in unstable positions above or beside basins.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:362:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:363:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:364:- Each water pixel falls straight down through bg cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:365:- When blocked below, it slides diagonally through the unique open side cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:366:- When resting on a surface, it slides horizontally toward the nearest gap where it can fall again.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:367:- Process repeats until no water pixel moves.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:368:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:369:Key insight: Water seeks the deepest reachable basin via diagonal and horizontal sliding, not just vertical fall.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:370:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:371:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:372:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:373:<reference_puzzle index="19" source="train" puzzle_id="984d8a3e" lines="5-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:374:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:375:Shift each row's dominant middle-color run left until its right edge aligns with the leftmost original right edge, moving displaced left-side pixels after the run.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:376:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:377:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:378:- The grid has three colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:379:- The most common color forms one contiguous horizontal run in every row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:380:- Pixels before those runs share one side color, and pixels after those runs share the other side color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:381:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:382:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:383:- Find the minimum right edge column among the middle-color runs.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:384:- In each row, keep the run width and the trailing right-side color count.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:385:- Place the middle-color run so its right edge is at that minimum column, unless the run is too wide, in which case start it at column 0.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:386:- Fill any remaining non-trailing cells with the left-side color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:387:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:388:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:389:The varying row prefixes are movable padding; the stable feature is the leftmost right boundary of the middle-color shape.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:390:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:391:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:392:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:393:<reference_puzzle index="20" source="eval" puzzle_id="b9e38dc0" lines="7-18">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:394:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:395:Fill the region enclosed by a wall sprite and radiate color outward through its opening.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:396:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:397:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:398:- bg = most common color. Wall = most frequent non-bg color, forming a partial enclosure (e.g. U-shape).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:399:- A fill-color pixel sits inside the enclosed area. Other non-bg pixels may act as obstacles.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:400:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:401:- Flood-fill the enclosed area with the fill color, radiating outward through the wall's open end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:402:- Obstacles cast "shadows" along the radiate direction, blocking fill behind them.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:403:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:404:Key insight: The wall endpoints define the opening direction; fill radiates outward through it, and obstacles block propagation along that same axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:405:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:406:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:407:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:408:你的任务：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:409:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:410:创新方式包括但不限于：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:411:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:412:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:413:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程"。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:414:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:415:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:416:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:417:<new_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:418:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:419:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:420:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed165869686/4/prompt.md:421:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。
